---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Set the thresholds" hint="A day of 20,000 uploads, 3% of them harmful. Move the two thresholds, the number of reviewers and the hash check, and watch the three kinds of cost: harmless content removed, harm that gets through, and reviewers who cannot keep up.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>At the <b>start</b> (remove at 0.90 or more, allow below 0.10, 5 reviewers) the review queue holds <b>2,284</b> items but 5 reviewers can do only <b>2,000</b>. <b>284</b> items are published unreviewed, <b>18</b> harmful items reach the public and <b>119</b> harmless uploads are removed by mistake.</li>
    <li>Raise <b>remove at</b> to <b>0.99</b>: wrongful removals fall from 119 to <b>6</b>, but the queue grows to 2,504 and <b>24</b> harmful items now get through, so being careful with removals moved the work to people.</li>
    <li>Then raise <b>reviewers to 20</b>: nothing overflows, only <b>12</b> harmful items remain (all scored below the allow line), and the wrongful removals stay at 6. Setting <b>hash matching off</b> adds work: more reaches the classifier and more harm is missed.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg cmb" data-cmb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Hash match on known-bad content <select class="pg-in" data-hash><option value="1" selected>on</option><option value="0">off</option></select></label>
      <label>Remove automatically at a score of <input type="range" min="50" max="99" value="90" data-hi /> <b data-hival></b></label>
      <label>Publish automatically below a score of <input type="range" min="5" max="80" step="5" value="10" data-lo /> <b data-loval></b></label>
      <label>Reviewers working each day <input type="range" min="1" max="20" value="5" data-rev /> <b data-revval></b></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Removed automatically</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Sent to human review</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Harm that reaches the public</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Precision and recall</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: a sample of 20,000 uploads with a deliberately weak classifier, so every effect shows, about 600 of them harmful, and a quarter of those are copies that the hash match knows. A harmless upload scores low, with a long tail, and a harmful one scores high, with a long tail the other way, so the two overlap in the middle. A reviewer handles 400 items a day, always the highest scores first, and is assumed to judge correctly. Items that do not fit are published unreviewed after their deadline. Red means more than 0.1% of harmless uploads were removed, or more than about 2.5% of the harmful ones got through (15), or the queue did not fit.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-cmb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const UPLOADS = 20000; const PREV = 0.03; const KNOWN = 0.25; const PER_REVIEWER = 400;
    const SEED = 77;
    const BAD_SKEW = 3; const OK_SKEW = 20; // classifier score shapes: harmful items cluster near 1, harmless near 0
    const WRONG_LIMIT = 0.001; const MISS_LIMIT = 0.025; // acceptable share of harmless items removed, of harm missed
    let seed = SEED; const rnd = () => ((seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296) / 4294967296);
    const items = Array.from({ length: UPLOADS }, () => {
      const bad = rnd() < PREV; const known = bad && rnd() < KNOWN; const u = rnd();
      return { bad, known, s: bad ? 1 - Math.pow(u, BAD_SKEW) : Math.pow(u, OK_SKEW) };
    });
    const totalBad = items.filter((i) => i.bad).length;
    function model(hi: number, lo: number, rev: number, hash: boolean) {
      let hashed = 0; let removedOk = 0; let removedWrong = 0; let missedLow = 0; const band: { bad: boolean; s: number }[] = [];
      for (const it of items) {
        if (hash && it.known) { hashed++; continue; }
        if (it.s >= hi) { if (it.bad) removedOk++; else removedWrong++; }
        else if (it.s >= lo) band.push(it);
        else if (it.bad) missedLow++;
      }
      band.sort((a, b) => b.s - a.s);
      const cap = rev * PER_REVIEWER; const over = band.slice(cap);
      const caught = band.slice(0, cap).filter((i) => i.bad).length;
      const missedOver = over.filter((i) => i.bad).length;
      const removedBad = hashed + removedOk + caught;
      return { hashed, removedOk, removedWrong, missedLow, missedOver, missed: missedLow + missedOver, band: band.length, cap, over: over.length, precision: removedBad / (removedBad + removedWrong), recall: removedBad / totalBad };
    }
    const fmt = (n: number) => Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-US');
    let pending = 0;
    function draw() {
      pending = 0;
      const hiRaw = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-hi]').value) / 100; const loRaw = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-lo]').value) / 100;
      const rev = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-rev]').value); const hash = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-hash]').value === '1';
      const lo = Math.min(loRaw, hiRaw);
      q('[data-hival]').textContent = hiRaw.toFixed(2); q('[data-loval]').textContent = loRaw.toFixed(2); q('[data-revval]').textContent = String(rev);
      const r = model(hiRaw, lo, rev, hash);
      const harmlessTotal = UPLOADS - totalBad;
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = `${fmt(r.hashed + r.removedOk + r.removedWrong)} items`;
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = `${fmt(r.hashed)} by hash match, ${fmt(r.removedOk + r.removedWrong)} by score, and ${fmt(r.removedWrong)} of those were harmless`;
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = `${fmt(r.band)} queued, room for ${fmt(r.cap)}`;
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = r.over > 0 ? `${fmt(r.over)} could not be reviewed in time and were published` : `all reviewed, ${fmt(r.cap - r.band)} places left`;
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = `${fmt(r.missed)} harmful items`;
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = `${fmt(r.missedLow)} scored below the publish line, ${fmt(r.missedOver)} waited in a full queue`;
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = `${Math.floor(r.precision * 100)}% and ${Math.floor(r.recall * 100)}%`;
      q('[data-n4]').textContent = 'precision: removals that were right. recall: harm that was removed';
      const wrongBad = r.removedWrong > harmlessTotal * WRONG_LIMIT; const missBad = r.missed > totalBad * MISS_LIMIT; const overBad = r.over > 0;
      const set = (id: string, bad: boolean) => q<HTMLElement>(id).style.setProperty('--c', bad ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      set('[data-b1]', wrongBad); set('[data-b2]', overBad); set('[data-b3]', missBad); set('[data-b4]', wrongBad || missBad);
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); const bad = wrongBad || missBad || overBad; out.classList.toggle('bad', bad);
      const parts: string[] = [];
      if (overBad) parts.push(`The queue holds ${fmt(r.band)} items for ${fmt(r.cap)} places, so ${fmt(r.over)} were published without a look.`);
      if (wrongBad) parts.push(`${fmt(r.removedWrong)} harmless uploads were removed automatically, which means ${fmt(r.removedWrong)} people to apologise to and appeals to handle.`);
      if (missBad) parts.push(`${fmt(r.missed)} harmful items got through.`);
      out.textContent = bad ? parts.join(' ') + ' Moving a threshold only moves the cost between wrong removals, missed harm and reviewer work. More reviewers is what lowers the missed harm without adding wrongful removals.'
        : `Balanced: ${fmt(r.removedWrong)} wrongful removals, ${fmt(r.missed)} harmful items missed and every queued item reviewed with ${fmt(r.cap - r.band)} places to spare.`;
    }
    const schedule = () => { if (!pending) pending = requestAnimationFrame(draw); };
    root.addEventListener('input', schedule); root.addEventListener('change', schedule);
    draw();
  });
</script>
